<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edward Elgar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Edward William Elgar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Edward Elgar was an English composer, born at Lower Broadheath near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/worcester">Worcester</a>, many of whose works entered the British and international concert repertoire. Self-taught, a Roman Catholic in Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and sensitive about his humble origins, he struggled for success until his forties, when the Enigma Variations (1899) became popular in Britain and abroad, followed by the choral work The Dream of Gerontius (1900). He also wrote the Pomp and Circumstance <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marches</a>, two symphonies and concertos for violin and cello, and was appointed Master of the King's Musick in 1924. Described as the first composer to take the gramophone seriously, he recorded most of his major orchestral works.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-elgar.jpg" alt="Edward Elgar" width="330" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edward_Elgar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Edward Elgar</b> re-scored it for very large orchestra for the Leeds Festival in 1922, and his version is the one usually heard at the Last Night of the Proms.</blockquote><a href="/songs/and-did-those-feet-in-ancient-time">Jerusalem (And did those feet in ancient time)</a></li><li><blockquote>The tune is the broad &quot;trio&quot; melody of <b>Edward Elgar</b>'s Pomp and Circumstance March No.</blockquote><a href="/songs/land-of-hope-and-glory">Land of Hope and Glory</a></li></ul></section>
